# Marketing Writer

Write marketing content that's casual, direct, and focused on real benefits—no corporate buzzwords or hype.

## Brand Voice Guidelines

### Core Principles

**Casual and direct:**
- Write like talking to a friend
- Use contractions (you're, it's, don't)
- Second person (you, your)
- Active voice

**No corporate speak:**
- Avoid: leverage, synergy, solution, ecosystem, empower, revolutionize
- Avoid: cutting-edge, game-changing, world-class, innovative
- Use: help, make, build, get, save

**Focus on real benefits:**
- Not: "Streamlines your workflow"
- Yes: "Saves you 2 hours a day"
- Not: "Optimizes productivity"
- Yes: "Get more done without the stress"

**Simple language:**
- Short sentences
- Common words
- No jargon unless necessary
- Explain technical terms simply

## Content Templates

### Landing Page Feature Section

**Format:** Problem → Solution → Benefit

```markdown
## [Feature Name - Keep it Simple]

[One sentence describing the problem this solves]

[2-3 sentences explaining how it works, in plain language]

[One sentence on the benefit/outcome]
```

**Example:**

```markdown
## Get Feedback Without the Back-and-Forth

Sending mockups via email and waiting for feedback kills momentum.

Share a link. Your client clicks on the design and leaves comments right there. You see them instantly.

Stop the email tennis. Ship designs faster.
```

### Tweet Thread

**Format:** Hook → Credibility → Value → CTA

**Structure:**
```
Tweet 1 (Hook):
[Relatable problem or bold claim that stops scrolling]

Tweet 2 (Build credibility):
[Why this matters / Why you should listen]

Tweet 3-4 (Show value):
[Specific examples or benefits]
[How it works / What makes it different]

Tweet 5 (CTA):
[Clear next step - try it, learn more, etc.]
```

### Launch Email

**Format:** Personal intro → Specific value → Easy CTA

```
Subject: [Direct, benefit-focused, < 50 chars]

Hey [name],

[Personal opening - 1 sentence acknowledging them]

[The problem - 1-2 sentences]

[What you built - 1-2 sentences, focus on benefit]

[How it works - 2-3 short sentences or bullets]

[Clear, easy CTA - what to do next]

[Casual sign-off]
```

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

### ❌ Using buzzwords
"Revolutionary AI-powered solution"

**Fix:** Describe what it actually does
"Uses AI to categorize your expenses automatically"

### ❌ Being vague about benefits
"Makes your workflow more efficient"

**Fix:** Be specific
"Cuts your weekly reporting from 3 hours to 10 minutes"

### ❌ Feature-dumping
"Includes advanced analytics, real-time sync, custom dashboards, API access..."

**Fix:** Focus on ONE main benefit per section
"See which features people use. Make better product decisions."

### ❌ Corporate language
"We're excited to announce..."

**Fix:** Talk like a person
"Made something that fixes this annoying problem..."

### ❌ Wall of text
Long paragraphs explaining every detail

**Fix:** Short sentences, white space, bullets
Break it up. Make it scannable.

## Review Checklist

Before sending any marketing content, verify:

- [ ] Sounds conversational (read it out loud)
- [ ] No buzzwords (leverage, synergy, revolutionize, etc.)
- [ ] Focuses on specific benefits, not vague claims
- [ ] Uses simple language (no jargon)
- [ ] Short sentences and paragraphs
- [ ] Explains how it works clearly
- [ ] Has clear CTA
- [ ] Feels authentic, not salesy

## Quick Reference: Word Swaps

| ❌ Don't Say | ✅ Say Instead |
|-------------|---------------|
| Leverage | Use |
| Solution | Tool / App |
| Revolutionize | Make easier / Fix |
| Cutting-edge | New / Modern |
| Synergy | Work together |
| Optimize | Improve / Make better |
| Empower | Help / Let you |
| Seamless | Easy / Simple |
| Robust | Reliable |
| Enterprise-grade | Professional / Serious |
| Game-changing | Really useful |
| Transform | Change / Improve |
| Innovative | Different / New |
| Ecosystem | Tools |

**When in doubt:** Use the simpler, more common word.
